### Kevalon ERP Module 3: Chart of Accounts (COA) Endpoints HTTP Requests Collection
# This file is compatible with VS Code REST Client extension.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000/api/coa
@accessToken = YOUR_ACCESS_TOKEN
@companyId = YOUR_COMPANY_ID
@accountId = YOUR_ACCOUNT_ID
@parentGroupId = YOUR_PARENT_GROUP_ID

### 1. Seed Default COA
# Seeds the standard hierarchical Chart of Accounts (Asset, Liability, Equity, Income, Expense)
POST {{baseUrl}}/seed-default
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

{
  "companyId": "{{companyId}}"
}


### 2. List Flat Chart of Accounts
# Returns a flat array of all accounts sorted by code ascending
GET {{baseUrl}}?companyId={{companyId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}


### 3. List Chart of Accounts as Nested Tree
# Returns a recursively nested tree structure for rendering an expandable account tree
GET {{baseUrl}}?companyId={{companyId}}&asTree=true
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}


### 4. Create Custom Account under a Seeded Group
# Creates a custom ledger or group account under a parent group (same company and type)
POST {{baseUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

{
  "companyId": "{{companyId}}",
  "name": "HDFC Bank - Current A/c",
  "type": "Asset",
  "isGroup": false,
  "parentId": "{{parentGroupId}}",
  "openingBalance": 15000.00,
  "openingBalanceType": "Dr"
}


### 5. Get Single Account Details
# Returns the account document including computed currentBalance
GET {{baseUrl}}/{{accountId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}


### 6. Update Account
# Reject changes to type and isGroup, reject modifications to name/code/parentId for system accounts.
PUT {{baseUrl}}/{{accountId}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

{
  "name": "Updated Account Name",
  "isActive": true
}


### 7. Delete Account
# Soft deletes (sets isActive: false) to prevent dangling historical references.
# Rejects if system account, group containing children, or account with transactions.
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/{{accountId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
